## In short

This policy explains what personal information Kariba Lake Connect collects, why, who sees it, how long we keep it, and your rights under Zimbabwe's Cyber and Data Protection Act [Chapter 12:07].

| What we collect | Why | How long |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Your account: name, email, phone, business name, role | To run your account and let you sign in | While your account is open, then deleted or anonymised 30 days after you ask us to delete it |
| Bookings: the name and phone for the booking, dates, group size, trip type, notes, price, deposit, status, reference | To pass your request to the operator, track it, and keep the records tax law requires | At least 6 years. If you delete your account, your name, phone and notes are removed from them |
| Reviews: your rating and comment, shown with your first name and trip month | To help other guests choose | While published. If you delete your account, your name becomes "Former guest" |
| Operator verification documents, including a director's identity document | To check that an operator is real and entitled to run its boats | Until you remove them or your account is deleted |
| Records of what you agreed to and when | To prove consent, as the law requires | Kept, with only your account number, the document version and the time |
| A security log of changes to bookings, listings and accounts | To keep the platform secure and settle disputes | Kept as a security record. Personal details are removed from it when an account is deleted |
| A sign-in token in your browser | To keep you signed in | Until you sign out or it expires |

We don't sell your personal information. We don't take payments, so we never hold your card or bank details.

## Who we are

**[Registered company name]** ("we", "us") runs Kariba Lake Connect and is the data controller for the personal information described here.

- Address: [Address]
- Email: privacy@[domain]
- Data Protection Officer: [Data Protection Officer name], privacy@[domain]
- Licensed by POTRAZ as a data controller, licence no. [ ]

The Postal and Telecommunications Regulatory Authority of Zimbabwe (POTRAZ) is Zimbabwe's Data Protection Authority.

## What this policy covers

This policy covers the Kariba Lake Connect website and everyone who uses it: visitors, guests, hotels and lodges, travel agencies, boat operators and their company members, and the captains operators register with us.

Boat operators are independent businesses. When an operator receives your booking details, the operator is responsible for how it uses them for your trip, under the same law.

## What we collect

**When you create an account (everyone):**

- your full name and email address;
- a password, which is stored only in scrambled (hashed) form by our sign-in provider;
- the kind of account you chose (guest, boat operator, hotel or lodge, or travel agency);
- your phone or WhatsApp number (required for operators and agencies, optional for guests); and
- your business name (operators, hotels and agencies).

**When you book a trip (guests, hotels and agencies):**

- the name and phone number of the person the booking is for;
- the date, time or number of days, group size and type of trip;
- any notes you write for the operator;
- the price, deposit and status of the booking, and its reference number; and
- that you accepted the booking liability waiver, with its version and the time.

If a hotel or agency books for you, it gives us your name and phone number. It must have your permission to do so.

**When you review a trip:** your overall rating, any category ratings, and your comment. Your first name and the month of the trip are added from your account and the booking.

**If you are a boat operator or company member:**

- your company's name, registration number, contact email and phone;
- the boats you list, their photos, registration numbers, prices, deposit and maintenance and operating-hours records;
- verification documents you upload: company registration, proof of boat ownership, operator licence and a director's identity document, with their labels and expiry dates, and our review decision and notes;
- the names and phone numbers of the captains you register, and which captain you assign to each booking; and
- your replies to reviews.

**If you are a hotel or travel agency:** the hotel or agency your account is linked to, and the bookings you make for guests.

**Records we create:**

- which version of our terms, privacy policy, operator agreement and booking waiver you accepted, and when, and whether you opted in to marketing messages;
- a security log of changes to accounts, bookings, listings, documents, reviews and other records, showing who made each change and when; and
- a verification status and trust score for partner accounts, set by our team.

**Collected automatically:**

- **A sign-in token** stored in your browser (see "Cookies and local storage").
- **Technical logs.** Our hosting provider, Supabase, records technical information about requests to our servers, such as IP address, browser type and time, to run and secure the service.
- **Images and fonts from other providers.** Some photographs on the website load from Unsplash (images.unsplash.com) and Pexels (images.pexels.com), and the typeface loads from Google Fonts (fonts.googleapis.com and fonts.gstatic.com). When your browser loads them, those providers receive your IP address and browser details, as with any website you visit. We don't send them anything else about you.

We don't use analytics or advertising trackers.

## Why we use it, and our lawful basis

The Cyber and Data Protection Act lets us process personal information with your consent, or without it where processing is needed to comply with the law, or for our legitimate interests where those are not overridden by your rights. You give your consent when you create an account and accept this policy, and again for each booking.

| Purpose | Information | Lawful basis |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Creating and running your account, letting you sign in | Account details | Your consent |
| Sending your booking request to the operator and managing it | Booking details | Your consent |
| Letting you and the operator track a booking | Reference, phone number, booking status | Your consent |
| Verifying operators and partners | Company details, verification documents | Your written consent (identity documents), and our legitimate interest in keeping guests safe |
| Publishing reviews and replies | Review, first name, trip month | Your consent |
| Keeping booking and financial records for tax | Booking and price records | Compliance with the law |
| Keeping the platform secure, preventing fraud, settling disputes | Security log, technical logs | Our legitimate interests |
| Recording what you agreed to | Consent records | Compliance with the law |
| Sending occasional updates and offers | Email or phone | Your consent, only if you opted in |

You don't have to give us your information, but without it we can't create your account or pass your booking to an operator.

## Sensitive information

We don't ask for health, religious, political or similar information. Please don't include it in booking notes or reviews.

A director's identity document, which operators upload to verify their company, is information we treat as sensitive. We process it only with the written consent you give by accepting this policy and choosing to upload it. It is stored in a private storage area that only you and our verification team can open. It is never shown to guests or other users. You can withdraw your consent at any time, free of charge, by asking us to remove the document; your company's verification will then lapse until a replacement is checked.

## Who we share it with

**The operator of the boat you book** receives the name and phone number for the booking, the dates, group size, trip type and your notes, so they can provide the trip.

**Guests** who book with an operator see the operator's business name and phone number, and the name and phone number of the captain assigned to their trip.

**Hotels and travel agencies** see the bookings made for their hotel or agency, including the guest details entered.

**The public** can see boat listings, including the operator's business name, phone number, the boat's registration number, verification status and trust score; and published reviews with the reviewer's first name and trip month. Other signed-in users can also see an operator account's name, phone number and business name.

**Anyone who has both a booking reference and the phone number used for it** can see that booking's status, boat, dates, group size and price on the Track a booking page, but not the guest's name or phone number.

**Our team** (administrators) can see accounts, bookings, documents and the security log to run, verify and support the platform.

**Service providers who process data for us:**

- **Supabase** hosts our database, user accounts and sign-in, and file storage, and sends account emails such as sign-up confirmation and password reset.
- **[Website hosting provider]** serves the website's pages.

They may use the information only on our instructions.

**Authorities**, such as the police, ZIMRA, POTRAZ or a court, when the law requires us to.

## Transfers outside Zimbabwe

Our database, sign-in and file storage are hosted by Supabase in the European Union, in Frankfurt, Germany (Supabase region eu-central-1). This means your personal information is transferred outside Zimbabwe.

The Cyber and Data Protection Act allows a transfer outside Zimbabwe when the recipient's country ensures an adequate level of protection, and the data is sent only so we can carry out our own tasks. We rely on:

- the protection given by the European Union's General Data Protection Regulation, which applies to Supabase's processing in Germany;
- our agreement with Supabase, which includes data processing terms requiring it to keep the data secure and use it only on our instructions; and
- the fact that the transfer is needed to perform our agreement with you, which the Act also allows.

The photograph and font providers listed above may receive your IP address on servers outside Zimbabwe when your browser loads their content.

## How we protect it

- Every request to our servers is encrypted in transit (HTTPS).
- Access rules in our database let each person see only the records their role allows; for example, an operator sees only bookings for their own boats.
- Verification documents are kept in private storage, not public links.
- Passwords are stored only in hashed form; we can't see them.
- Changes to important records are written to a security log that can't be edited through the website.
- Our team accounts are limited to the people who need them.

No system is completely secure. Please use a strong password that you don't use anywhere else.

## Data breaches

If a security breach affects personal information we hold, we will report it to POTRAZ within 24 hours of becoming aware of it, as the Cyber and Data Protection Act and its 2024 regulations require. If the breach is likely to put your rights and freedoms at high risk, we will also tell you within 72 hours, explain what happened and what you can do. We keep a record of every breach.

## How long we keep it

We keep personal information only as long as we need it for the purposes above.

| Information | How long |
| --- | --- |
| Account details | While your account is open. Deleted or anonymised 30 days after you ask us to delete your account |
| Booking and payment records | At least 6 years, because Zimbabwe's tax laws require businesses to keep their records for at least six years. After your account is deleted they are kept with your name, phone number and notes removed |
| Reviews | While published. After your account is deleted, shown as "Former guest" |
| Verification documents | Until you remove them, or your account is deleted |
| Captains' details | Until the operator's team removes them. If the operator who added them deletes their account, they stay on the team's roster; if no one else is on the team, they are deleted |
| Consent records | Kept as proof of what was agreed. They contain only an account number, document version and time |
| Security log | Kept as a security record. Names, phone numbers and other personal details are removed from it when the related account is deleted |
| Sign-in token in your browser | Until you sign out or it expires |

## Deleting your account

You can ask us to delete your account at any time from **Account** in the menu at the top of the page.

1. **Day 0.** You confirm the request. We show you the date your account will be deleted, 30 days later.
2. **Days 1 to 30.** Nothing is deleted yet. You can still sign in, and you can cancel the deletion at any time. We remind you each time you sign in.
3. **After 30 days**, we delete or anonymise your personal information:
   - your name, phone number and business name are removed from your account, and you can no longer sign in; your sign-in record is deleted, or, where other records still point to it, emptied of your email, phone and password and permanently blocked;
   - verification documents you uploaded are deleted, and the files removed from storage;
   - captains you registered stay on your team's roster if anyone else is on your team; if you operate alone, they are deleted and their names and phone numbers removed from past trips on your boats;
   - on bookings you made, your name becomes "Former guest" and your phone number and notes are removed; the reference, boat, dates and amounts are kept for tax records;
   - reviews you wrote stay published as "Former guest";
   - if you operate boats as part of a team, the boats you hold pass to another member of your team (another owner first; otherwise the longest-serving manager or staff member, who becomes an owner); if you operate alone, your listings are taken down;
   - names, phone numbers and other personal details are removed from the security log entries about your records.

If you still have an active booking that has not happened yet when the 30 days end, we wait until it is completed or cancelled, then delete your account. For an operator on a team, a booking on a boat only causes this wait when no one else on the team can take the boat over.

Records of what you agreed to are kept, with only your account number, as proof of consent.

## Your rights

Under the Cyber and Data Protection Act you have the right to:

- **be informed** of how your personal information is used (this policy);
- **access** the personal information we hold about you;
- **object** to the processing of all or part of your personal information;
- have **false or misleading information corrected**; and
- have **false or misleading information deleted**.

You can also:

- **withdraw your consent** at any time, including consent to marketing and to processing of sensitive information, free of charge;
- **delete your account**, as described above; and
- **ask for a person to review** anything that happens automatically. Some things happen automatically under fixed rules: for example, a listing is hidden while its maintenance is overdue, and a company's verified status lapses when a required document expires.

Operators can update their company's details in the operator portal. For any other correction, email us.

To use any of these rights, email privacy@[domain] from the email address on your account. We may ask you to confirm your identity. We will respond within 30 days, and it is free. If someone acts for you, for example a parent or guardian, or a person appointed by law, we will ask for proof that they may.

**Complaints.** If you are unhappy with how we handle your information, please tell us first at privacy@[domain]. You also have the right to complain to the Data Protection Authority:

